symmetry-map-85aad343.conceptual_definition:
The equation describes the curl of a vector field 

 in cylindrical coordinates. Specifically, it calculates the rotational component of the vector field 

, which is represented by the vector potential 

, in terms of its components along the radial (

), azimuthal (

), and axial (

) directions. The determinant expansion provides a systematic way to compute this curl in this non-Cartesian coordinate system.
